-<p><em>Ezra 1–2</em></p>
 <h2>A Mission and a Role</h2>
 <h2>Introduction</h2>
 <p>In my introductory sermon a couple weeks ago we saw that the story of Ezra Nehemiah is much like our own. God called them out of exile in Persia to build his temple and city. They were opposed by their enemies and fought them off with God's help. Likewise, we have been called out of exile to sin and death so that we can build the temple and the city--which is the church. We are promised persecution. But because God has made a new, better, stronger covenent with us this chapter of the story will not end in tragedy and compromise. It will end with all things made new, the church as a spotless bride, the city of God expanding as the increase of Christ's government has no end, and even death swallowed up in victory.</p>
